    "caption": "The tracking server is stateless: metadata goes to a database, files go to object storage, and serving code finds the right model through a registry alias.",
    "alt": "Training jobs and LLM apps log runs, metrics, models and traces to the MLflow tracking server. The server writes metadata such as runs, metrics and registry entries to a SQL backend store, and proxies artifacts such as model files to an object storage bucket. A serving process asks the server to resolve models:/name@champion to a specific version, then loads that version's files from the bucket.",
